 "notes": {
  "I5": "The shelf first opening at 1440x900 dpr 2 CPU 4x: every growing frame set the canvas width and height (two buffer allocations, measured 4 to 9 ms a frame at 4x, 2 to 3 ms each), and from about 680 ms the frames ran at half rate (7 frames at 33 ms); the 83 ms frame of the earlier run was not reproduced in 20 runs (a GPU or machine stall on top of the same allocations is the likely cause). Fixed by a coarse buffer: while the frame moves the buffer is allocated only when the need passes it or is 256 device px under it, and ends at the window size so the end allocates nothing (frame-math coarseBuffer, FrameOptions.coarse, shelf-frame applyView). First opening: max 16.8 ms, 0 frames over 20 ms, in 3 of 3 runs and 6 of 6 profile runs.",
  "plainGrid": "the plain grid is glued to the frame (the window-sized grid, scaled and centred) at full opacity from the first move row (gridInFirstMoveRows); the first two film frames (13 to 33 ms) still show the box ground while the new composited layer rasters (a compositor latency; no frame is empty after the first 50 ms: emptyAfter50ms 0)",
  "reducedMotion": "a dip through dark: the black rises over the page over the first 100 ms with the scene in its box, then the scene is carried and the open page fades in over the second 100 ms (no growing frame; no scene carried while the page is lit); the 0.9 bar allows for the 0.01 ms transition the reduced-motion stylesheet gives everything (a computed style read in the frame the driver wrote it still has the old value: one run of four showed one such row, shade 0.87 with the scene at 3.7% opacity, and one wall close took 363 ms instead of 184 to 201, not reproduced in the other three)",
  "wallPhoneEmpty": "the phone wall film is judged with the wall given 6 s to load its thumbnails (a wall of grey placeholders is flat to the empty-frame check; with a slow network it failed in 3 of 3 runs before the wait, 0 empty frames in 2 of 2 after)"
 }
}
